{"content":[{"c":["HAND"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The terminal part of the forelimb that has the ability to grasp. “Hand” is used hundreds of times in the Bible to describe a physical part of one’s body. It is also used frequently in metaphors or figurative language."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Figuratively, the hand meant power (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.2.15","r":"Deut.2.15","rawR":"Deut.2.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.2.15","value":"Deut.2.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 2:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.31.5","r":"Ps.31.5","rawR":"Ps.31.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.31.5","value":"Ps.31.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 31:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.14.62","r":"Mark.14.62","rawR":"Mark.14.62","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.14.62","value":"Mark.14.62"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 14:62"},"). Indeed, in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.8.20","r":"Josh.8.20","rawR":"Josh.8.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.8.20","value":"Josh.8.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 8:20"}," “hand to flee” is translated “power to flee” (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.76.5","r":"Ps.76.5","rawR":"Ps.76.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.76.5","value":"Ps.76.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 76:5"},"). Conversely, limp hands symbolized irresoluteness and weakness (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.35.3","r":"Isa.35.3","rawR":"Isa.35.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.35.3","value":"Isa.35.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 35:3"},"). Clasping the hands signified friendship (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.10.15","r":"2Kgs.10.15","rawR":"2Kgs.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.10.15","value":"2Kgs.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 10:15"},"). To seat someone on one’s right hand denoted favor (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.16.11","r":"Ps.16.11","rawR":"Ps.16.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.16.11","value":"Ps.16.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 16:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.77.10","r":"Ps.77.10","rawR":"Ps.77.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.77.10","value":"Ps.77.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"77:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.1","r":"Ps.110.1","rawR":"Ps.110.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.1","value":"Ps.110.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:1"},"). Clean hands symbolized innocence (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.26.6","r":"Ps.26.6","rawR":"Ps.26.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.26.6","value":"Ps.26.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 26:6"},"), while striking hands sealed a bargain (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.6.1","r":"Pr.6.1","rawR":"Pr.6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.6.1","value":"Pr.6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 6:1"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Lifting the hand symbolized violence (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.11.26","r":"1Kgs.11.26","rawR":"1Kgs.11.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.11.26","value":"1Kgs.11.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 11:26"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The hands were used in supplicatory prayer (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.17.11","r":"Exod.17.11","rawR":"Exod.17.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.17.11","value":"Exod.17.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 17:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.9.22","r":"Lev.9.22","rawR":"Lev.9.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.9.22","value":"Lev.9.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 9:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.1.15","r":"Isa.1.15","rawR":"Isa.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.1.15","value":"Isa.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 1:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.2.8","r":"1Tim.2.8","rawR":"1Tim.2.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.2.8","value":"1Tim.2.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 2:8"},") and in making vows (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.22","r":"Gen.14.22","rawR":"Gen.14.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.22","value":"Gen.14.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:22"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.2","r":"Gen.24.2","rawR":"Gen.24.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.2","value":"Gen.24.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Other idiomatic uses of the hands expressed jeopardizing one’s life (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.3","r":"Judg.12.3","rawR":"Judg.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.3","value":"Judg.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 12:3"},"), gladness (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.11.12","r":"2Kgs.11.12","rawR":"2Kgs.11.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.11.12","value":"2Kgs.11.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 11:12"},"), generosity (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.15.11","r":"Deut.15.11","rawR":"Deut.15.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.15.11","value":"Deut.15.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 15:11"},"), grief (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.13.19","r":"2Sam.13.19","rawR":"2Sam.13.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.13.19","value":"2Sam.13.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 13:19"},"), humility (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.30.32","r":"Pr.30.32","rawR":"Pr.30.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.30.32","value":"Pr.30.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 30:32"},"), and undertaking a duty (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.9.62","r":"Luke.9.62","rawR":"Luke.9.62","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.9.62","value":"Luke.9.62"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 9:62"},"). Manual labor is an expression of man’s dignity and duty (",{"href":"?bref=Eph.4.28","r":"Eph.4.28","rawR":"Eph.4.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.4.28","value":"Eph.4.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 4:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.4.11","r":"1Thes.4.11","rawR":"1Thes.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.4.11","value":"1Thes.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 4:11"},"), the marks of which Paul was not ashamed to display (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.20.34","r":"Acts.20.34","rawR":"Acts.20.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.20.34","value":"Acts.20.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 20:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.4.12","r":"1Cor.4.12","rawR":"1Cor.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.4.12","value":"1Cor.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 4:12"},"). Ritual hand washing was obligatory for the priests before fulfilling their office (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.30.19-21","r":"Exod.30.19-21","rawR":"Exod.30.19-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.30.19-21","value":"Exod.30.19-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 30:19-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.40.30-32","r":"Exod.40.30-32","rawR":"Exod.40.30-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.40.30-32","value":"Exod.40.30-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"40:30-32"},"). The scribes and Pharisees so misapplied this that Jesus ignored ceremonial hand washing (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.15.1-20","r":"Matt.15.1-20","rawR":"Matt.15.1-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.15.1-20","value":"Matt.15.1-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 15:1-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.11.38","r":"Luke.11.38","rawR":"Luke.11.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.11.38","value":"Luke.11.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 11:38"},"). Pilate’s hand washing (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.24","r":"Matt.27.24","rawR":"Matt.27.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.24","value":"Matt.27.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:24"},") disclaimed responsibility for, or professed innocence concerning, a wrong that, however, could not be done without his consent."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["When Israel went out of Egypt “with an high hand” (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.14.8","r":"Exod.14.8","rawR":"Exod.14.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.14.8","value":"Exod.14.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 14:8"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), the reference is to the hand or help of the Lord. The hand of the Lord represented God’s resistless power (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.2.15","r":"Deut.2.15","rawR":"Deut.2.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.2.15","value":"Deut.2.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 2:15"},"), judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.13.11","r":"Acts.13.11","rawR":"Acts.13.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.13.11","value":"Acts.13.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 13:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.31","r":"Heb.10.31","rawR":"Heb.10.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.31","value":"Heb.10.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 10:31"},"), divine inspiration (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.8.1","r":"Ezek.8.1","rawR":"Ezek.8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.8.1","value":"Ezek.8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 8:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.37.1","r":"Ezek.37.1","rawR":"Ezek.37.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.37.1","value":"Ezek.37.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"37:1"},"), and providential care (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.6","r":"Ezra.7.6","rawR":"Ezra.7.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.6","value":"Ezra.7.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.10.28-29","r":"John.10.28-29","rawR":"John.10.28-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.28-29","value":"John.10.28-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 10:28-29"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The laying on of hands had a profound significance and occurs frequently in the Bible. Before making a blood sacrifice, the person making the offering, not the priest, laid hands on the victim. The act signified the transference of guilt to, or self-identification with, the victim (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.1.4","r":"Lev.1.4","rawR":"Lev.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.1.4","value":"Lev.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 1:4"},"). Laying on of hands signified appointment to an office, as when Moses commissioned Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Num.27.12-23","r":"Num.27.12-23","rawR":"Num.27.12-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.27.12-23","value":"Num.27.12-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 27:12-23"},"), the apostles made seven disciples their associates or deputies in the ministry (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.5-6","r":"Acts.6.5-6","rawR":"Acts.6.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.5-6","value":"Acts.6.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 6:5-6"},"), and Paul and Barnabas were appointed missionaries and representatives of the church in Antioch (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.13.3","r":"Acts.13.3","rawR":"Acts.13.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.13.3","value":"Acts.13.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:3"},"). By laying on of hands, a person was made an associate with the holder of an office and was admitted to the status of that office (",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.4.14","r":"1Tim.4.14","rawR":"1Tim.4.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.4.14","value":"1Tim.4.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 4:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.1.6","r":"2Tim.1.6","rawR":"2Tim.1.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.1.6","value":"2Tim.1.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 1:6"},"). The act was accompanied by prayer and was, in itself, a form of prayer. As Augustine remarks: “What else is the laying on of hands but a prayer over one?”"],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The laying on of hands accompanied healing in the ministry of the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.6.5","r":"Mark.6.5","rawR":"Mark.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.6.5","value":"Mark.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 6:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.40","r":"Luke.4.40","rawR":"Luke.4.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.40","value":"Luke.4.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 4:40"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.13.11-13","r":"Luke.13.11-13","rawR":"Luke.13.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.13.11-13","value":"Luke.13.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:11-13"},") and of the disciples (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.16.18","r":"Mark.16.18","rawR":"Mark.16.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.16.18","value":"Mark.16.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 16:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.9.12,17","r":"Acts.9.12,17","rawR":"Acts.9.12,17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.9.12,17","value":"Acts.9.12,17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 9:12, 17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.28.8","r":"Acts.28.8","rawR":"Acts.28.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.28.8","value":"Acts.28.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:8"},"). This expressed the self-identification and sympathy of the healer with and for the sufferer, as well as reinforced the patient’s faith and God’s imparting health to him in answer to prayer."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=RightHand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"RightHand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"RightHand_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Right Hand"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hand","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 2:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.2.15","rawQueryValue":"Deut.2.15","sourceRefExact":"Deut.2.15"},{"anchorText":"Ps 31:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.31.5","rawQueryValue":"Ps.31.5","sourceRefExact":"Ps.31.5"},{"anchorText":"Mk 14:62","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.14.62","rawQueryValue":"Mark.14.62","sourceRefExact":"Mark.14.62"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 8:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.8.20","rawQueryValue":"Josh.8.20","sourceRefExact":"Josh.8.20"},{"anchorText":"Ps 76:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.76.5","rawQueryValue":"Ps.76.5","sourceRefExact":"Ps.76.5"},{"anchorText":"Is 35:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.35.3","rawQueryValue":"Isa.35.3","sourceRefExact":"Isa.35.3"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 10:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.10.15","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.10.15","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.10.15"},{"anchorText":"Pss 16:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.16.11","rawQueryValue":"Ps.16.11","sourceRefExact":"Ps.16.11"},{"anchorText":"77:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.77.10","rawQueryValue":"Ps.77.10","sourceRefExact":"Ps.77.10"},{"anchorText":"110:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.110.1","rawQueryValue":"Ps.110.1","sourceRefExact":"Ps.110.1"},{"anchorText":"Ps 26:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.26.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.26.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.26.6"},{"anchorText":"Prv 6:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.6.1","rawQueryValue":"Pr.6.1","sourceRefExact":"Pr.6.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 11:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.11.26","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.11.26","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.11.26"},{"anchorText":"Ex 17:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.17.11","rawQueryValue":"Exod.17.11","sourceRefExact":"Exod.17.11"},{"anchorText":"Lv 9:22","canonicalization":"de